  solution: Vale had been stealing from the royal treasury for a year, and borrowed
    four hundred crowns from Lady Seraphine to hide the gap. When Lord Halvard drafted
    the Queen's decree ordering an audit at dawn, Vale knew he was finished. After
    the third bell he slipped out of the library, took Master Ilric's wolfsbane from
    the unlocked cabinet, signed out the cellar key in his own green ink, and poisoned
    the Queen's private cask while the cellar patrol was away. His order slip made
    sure that cask, and only that cask, would be poured for the vesper toast.
  durationSeconds: 600
